<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Excel-DNA add-in descriptor. Read by Excel when it loads the .xll.

  RuntimeVersion="v4.0" matches our net48 target. The CLR Bridge will load
  this assembly and call AddIn.AutoOpen()/AutoClose() at the appropriate
  lifecycle points. See PyExcel.Addin.AddIn.cs for those entry points.

  ## What this file lists

  Only assemblies that Excel-DNA must SCAN at load time for [ExcelRibbon]
  / [ExcelFunction] / [ExcelCommand] entry points belong here as
  <ExternalLibrary>. Today that's:

    * PyExcel.Addin.dll  — IExcelAddIn (AutoOpen / AutoClose)
    * PyExcel.Ribbon.dll — PyExcelRibbon (CustomUI ribbon callbacks)
    * PyExcel.Excel.dll  — PyRunFunction (=PY.RUN UDF)

  ## Where the rest of the assemblies come from

  Every other DLL the .xll needs at runtime (PyExcel.Common /.State /.Bridge
  /.Kernel.Client /.Setup, plus Apache.Arrow and its System.* polyfills) is
  picked up by the `PackedReferences` MSBuild target in
  PyExcel.Addin.csproj, which globs every .dll in $(OutDir) into
  ExcelAddInInclude before ExcelDnaBuild runs. That avoids hand-listing
  each transitive dependency here — adding a new ProjectReference or
  PackageReference automatically rides along.

  ## History

  An earlier comment here ("a merely-referenced dependency is packed for
  runtime loading but NOT scanned") was wrong. ExcelDnaPack only embeds
  assemblies that are explicitly named (here as <ExternalLibrary>, or
  via ExcelAddInInclude). Without that, the packed .xll references types
  that aren't in its manifest and FileNotFoundException fires at load —
  symptom: "Could not load file or assembly 'PyExcel.Common, …'" the
  first time Excel-DNA instantiates PyExcelRibbon. The .csproj glob
  fixes that by including everything that lands next to the .xll.
-->
<DnaLibrary Name="PyExcel" RuntimeVersion="v4.0">
  <ExternalLibrary Path="PyExcel.Addin.dll"
                   ExplicitExports="false"
                   LoadFromBytes="true"
                   Pack="true" />
  <ExternalLibrary Path="PyExcel.Ribbon.dll"
                   ExplicitExports="false"
                   LoadFromBytes="true"
                   Pack="true" />
  <ExternalLibrary Path="PyExcel.Excel.dll"
                   ExplicitExports="false"
                   LoadFromBytes="true"
                   Pack="true" />
</DnaLibrary>
